<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Port Moresby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded <a href="/years/1873">1873</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Port Moresby is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>, on the south coast of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>. Named in 1873 by the British naval officer John Moresby, it was the seat of British New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> from 1884 and then of the Australian Territory of Papua. A major Allied base in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, it became the capital of independent Papua New Guinea in 1975.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/port-moresby.jpg" alt="Port Moresby" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MSchlauch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Port_Moresby_Town2_Mschlauch.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
